nator John McCAIN \u2013 says Palin will do fine.]  \n\n(Studio: Brian Williams; St. Louis: Chuck Todd) The goals for each candidate, the electoral map and McCain\u2019s decision to focus on Pennsylvania and Wisconsin rather than Michigan discussed. ", "segment_duration": 310, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 919855, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "4Xy47DW6S3", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-02", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 919854, "segment_id": "S184Q7ZyJl", "segment_broadcast_id": "4Xy47DW6S3", "segment_title": "Economy: Bailout Bill / House Vote", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) Stock Market Report.   (Capitol: Tom Costello) The push to get the economic bailout package passed in the House featured; statistics on jobless claims and factory orders cited; details given about the pork included in the bill. [Speaker of the House Nancy PELOSI \u2013 says she is optimistic that we will take a bill to the floor.] [Representatives John SHADEGG&#134;, Roy BLUNT&#134;, Emanuel CLEAVER&#134;&#134;- offer views.] [President BUSH \u2013 says the House must listen.] [Representative Barney FRANK&#134;- says we may have to vote for this with their obnoxious revisions.] [Representative Ted POE&#134;- questions the tax breaks.] ", "segment_duration": 180, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63360.0", "legacy_segment_id": 919856, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_na